@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Announcement}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Announcement @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Announcement @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</h1>

<p>
    The Announcement History component is part of the BlazorRamp.Core NuGet package and allows the user to view a rolling list of the 20 announcement made via a live region service
    which populate a hidden page element that is marked with the ARIA live attribute.
</p>
<p>
    An ARIA live region is a designated area of a page that assistive technologies such as screen readers monitor for changes. When content within a live region is updated dynamically, 
    the change is automatically announced to the user without them needing to navigate to that part of the page. This makes live regions particularly useful for communicating status messages, 
    notifications, alerts, and other time-sensitive information that appears outside of the user's current focus.
</p>
<p>
    This component was primarily designed for screen reader users, as transient announcements made via live regions cam be misheard or get clipped by the screen reader, and thus provides
    a mechanism for the user to be able to replay these announcements if necessary.
</p>
<p>
    The announcement history viewer is a non-modal dialog that can be accessed at any time by using the shortcut keys <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>H</kbd> or by clicking
    on its associated button, which can either remain visible all the time or only when it is focused <span class="code-span">:focus-visible</span>.
</p>
<p>
   On this site the announcement history component has been configured to show its associated button, labelled as Alerts, appearing at the bottom left corner of the screen.
</p>
<p>
    The theme switch at the top right of the page, as well as the busy indicator component makes use of the live region service to make announcements via live regions (elements part of the component) and as such as an example, 
    if you toggle the site theme and/or test the busy indicator (from its overview page) announcements will be logged and available for review using the announcement history viewer.
</p>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Accordion}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Accordion - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Announcement}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Announcement - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
